-- title:
--   Lifting idempotents mod p with stable p-torsion in Čech H¹
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring and let $\mathcal{U}$ be a two-chart cover over $R$ in the sense of the project: three commutative $R$-algebras $A_0$, $A_1$, $A_{01}$ together with $R$-algebra maps $\rho_0 : A_0 \to A_{01}$ and $\rho_1 : A_1 \to A_{01}$. Let $p \in R$ and $n \in \mathbb{N}$. The structure sheaf of $\mathcal{U}$ is the system of sections with $M_0 = A_0$, $M_1 = A_1$, $M_{01} = A_{01}$ and restriction maps $\rho_0$ and $1 \cdot \rho_1$ (the line bundle attached to the unit transition function $1$), and `𝒰.structureSheaf.H1` is its first Čech cohomology, the $R$-module $A_{01}$ modulo the submodule of differences $\rho_1(b) - \rho_0(a)$ with $a \in A_0$, $b \in A_1$. Assume the $p$-power torsion of this module stabilises at $n$: for every $x$ in it, $p^{n+1} \cdot x = 0$ implies $p^{n} \cdot x = 0$. Assume further given $c_0 \in A_0$ and $c_1 \in A_1$ that are idempotent modulo $p$, i.e. $c_0^2 - c_0$ lies in the ideal generated by the image of $p$ in $A_0$ and $c_1^2 - c_1$ in the ideal generated by the image of $p$ in $A_1$, and that agree modulo $p$ on the overlap, i.e. $\rho_0(c_0) - \rho_1(c_1)$ lies in the ideal generated by the image of $p$ in $A_{01}$. Then there are $a_0 \in A_0$ and $a_1 \in A_1$ with $\rho_0(a_0) = \rho_1(a_1)$ such that $a_0 - c_0$ and $a_1 - c_1$ lie in the ideals generated by the image of $p$ in $A_0$ and in $A_1$ respectively. Note that the conclusion asserts only agreement of $a_0$ and $a_1$ on the overlap and congruence with $c_0$, $c_1$ modulo $p$; it does not assert that $a_0$, $a_1$ are idempotent.
--
--   This is the degree-zero content of the theorem on formal functions in an elementary two-chart form: an idempotent function given modulo $p$ on each chart, compatible on the overlap, is the reduction of a genuine global section, which is the algebraic input to Zariski's connectedness principle. It is used in the proofs of connectedness of the fibres of the two-chart integral model of a curve and of the corresponding pullback for the Igusa scheme.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_TwoChartCech_Cover_exists_overlap_eq_sub_mem_span_of_H1_torsion_stable.lean

